      "level": 2,
      "content": "Montane Forest Altitudinal Zones"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Montane forests in India display distinct altitudinal zonation matching changes in temperature and rainfall.",
        "Wet temperate forests dominate elevations between 1,000 and 2,000 meters, characterised by evergreen broad-leaf species like oak and chestnut.",
        "Temperate coniferous forests (1,500m to 3,000m) contain economically vital species such as Deodar, Pine, Spruce, and Cedar.",
        "Mangroves are halophytic plant communities adapted to saline, oxygen-deprived tidal estuaries and mudflats.",
        "Key mangrove survival adaptations include pneumatophores (breathing roots), salt-excreting leaves, and viviparous seed germination."
      ],
      "id": "lf939tm"
    },
    {
